+# Slice 3.RV-review-ipc — the window's review source: threads and GitLab through `RangeSource`
+
+Board "Review a commit range" row 19 (B; needs row 17's generated bindings, row 18's `ipc/threadLine.ts`, row 8's
+`RangeSource`). Product rules: `docs/plan.md` §2 **#116**–**#120** — read them. Design:
+`.omp/run/notes/ThreadsDesign.md` "7. IPC" ("Window side": `ipc/threadLine.ts`, brands, `ipc/reviewDomain.ts`,
+`ReviewSource`, `RangeSource extends SettingsSource, ReviewSource`), "Fixture mode" (`ipc/fixtureReview.ts`, the
+`?threads=seeded` and `?gitlab=<script>` scripts), "8. Tests" (`reviewDomain.test.ts`, `fixtureReview.test.ts`). Row
+20 (the window's thread state) builds on this surface.
+
+Facts (given):
+
+- Row 17 generated in `bindings.ts`: `ThreadId`, `MessageId`, `ThreadLine`, `MessageBody`, `Posting`, `Message`,
+  `Thread`, `ThreadList`, `ThreadAdded`, `MergeRequestRef`, `LookedAt`, `NotLinedUp`, `GitLabCheck`, `SendProgress`,
+  `SendReply`; `IpcError` gains `UnknownThread`, `UnknownMessage`, `EmptyMessage`, `MessagePending`, `SendRunning`;
+  `commands.listThreads`, `addThread`, `addNote`, `queueMessage`, `unqueueMessage`, `checkGitlab`,
+  `sendQueue(progress: TAURI_CHANNEL<SendProgress>)`.
+- Row 18 added `ipc/threadLine.ts` (the domain `ThreadLine` with `LeftLine`/`RightLine` brands, `shownColumn`).
+- Row 8's pattern (after its fix round): `RangeSource`, `rangeDomain.ts`, `tauriRange.ts` (+ test), `fixtureRange.ts`
+  (shared `DIFFERENCE`, `parsedCases`, `memberOf` from `fixture.ts`); `createTauriServerHost` shows a `Channel` per
+  call (`ipc/tauri.ts`).
+- `ui/problemText.ts` maps every `IpcError` kind (an exhaustive switch; the new kinds break the type check until
+  handled).
+
+## Target
+
+Owned: `frontend/src/ipc/{ReviewSource,reviewDomain,reviewDomain.test,tauriReview,tauriReview.test,fixtureReview,
+fixtureReview.test}.ts` (new), `frontend/src/ipc/{domain,threadLine,RangeSource,tauriRange,fixtureRange,
+fixtureRange.test,index}.ts`, `frontend/src/ipc/AGENTS.md`, `frontend/src/ui/{problemText,problemText.test}.ts`,
+`scripts/map-check.sh`.
+
+Read-only: everything else.
+
+Non-goals: the store, components, editor.
+
+## Contract (fixed; you may add, never change)
+
+```ts
+// ipc/domain.ts: ThreadId, MessageId brands by type guard (IPC3)
+// ipc/threadLine.ts: toThreadLine(raw) / fromThreadLine(line) between the generated and the domain shape
+// ipc/reviewDomain.ts: camelCase shapes (draftNote, mergeRequest, webUrl, lookedAt, shortId, gitlabHead, …) and
+//   toThreadList, toThreadAdded, toGitLabCheck, toSendReply
+// ipc/ReviewSource.ts
+export interface ReviewSource {
+  listThreads(): Promise<SourceResult<ThreadList>>;
+  addThread(file: RangeFileId, line: ThreadLine, text: string): Promise<SourceResult<ThreadAdded>>;
+  addNote(thread: ThreadId, text: string): Promise<SourceResult<ThreadList>>;
+  queueMessage(message: MessageId, text: string): Promise<SourceResult<ThreadList>>;
+  unqueueMessage(message: MessageId): Promise<SourceResult<ThreadList>>;
+  checkGitLab(): Promise<SourceResult<GitLabCheck>>;
+  sendQueue(onProgress: (progress: SendProgress) => void): Promise<SourceResult<SendReply>>;
+}
+// ipc/RangeSource.ts: interface RangeSource extends SettingsSource, ReviewSource { openRange; loadRangeFile }
+// createTauriRangeSource / createFixtureRangeSource include the review methods (tauriReview.ts / fixtureReview.ts)
+// fixture: threads in memory; ?threads=seeded (one thread of each ThreadLine kind on the review case, plus one queued,
+// one refused, one pending and one aiAnswer message); ?gitlab=<script>: linedUp (default), checking (answers after
+// 3 s), noGlab, loggedOut, noMergeRequest, noBranch, moved, otherBase, several, preparing, failed, refusal (the
+// second queued message refused: "400 Bad request - Note {:line_code=>[\"can't be blank\"]}"), stopped (a timeout
+// after the first); progress per message with a 300 ms pause
+```
+
+`ui/problemText.ts`: a fixed reason for each new kind; `scripts/map-check.sh`: the loop gains `ReviewSource`.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+`reviewDomain.test.ts` (every arm of `Posting`, `MessageBody`, `NotLinedUp`, `LookedAt`, `SendReply`; bad ids refused
+by the brands), `tauriReview.test.ts` (camelCasing, failures unchanged, progress through the channel),
+`fixtureReview.test.ts` (each script; `seeded`), `problemText.test.ts` (the new reasons). Your tests kill the mutants
+on your lines (Stryker, SP5).
+
+Commands: `pnpm -C frontend typecheck`, `pnpm -C frontend lint`, `pnpm -C frontend test`, `pnpm -C frontend fmt:check`.
+
+## Skills
+
+`skill://ts-conventions`, `skill://ipc-contract` (plus your autoloaded ones).
